Q: Casting in comparator functions for qsort A: <p>Consider sorting an array of type <code>D arr[]</code>.  <code>int cmp(const void *a, const void *b)</code> provides pointers <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>.  Each points to an element of the array <code>D[]</code>: &quot;... with two arguments that point to the objects being compared.&quot;   So each should be converted to a <code>D *</code>.</p>
<pre><code>// Step 1
int cmp(const void *a, const void *b){
    D *pa=a;
    D *pb=b;
    //do something
}
</code></pre>
<p>As type <code>D</code> is certainly not a <code>const</code> type, else attempting to sort the array is foolish (likely UB), and the pointers <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> point to <code>const</code> data, we should continue that <code>const</code>-ness.</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>// Step 2
int cmp(const void *a, const void *b){
    const D *pa = a;
    const D *pb = b;
    //do something
}
</code></pre>
<p>As OP has the type <code>D</code> as <code>T *^n</code>, then</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>// Step 3
int cmp(const void *a,const void *b){
    const T *^n *pa=a;
    const T *^n *pb=b;
    //do something
}
</code></pre>

Q: Setting FILE_ATTRIBUTE_PINNED / UNPINNED makes file Hidden and System A: <p><code>PinFile()</code> is using the bitwise <code>and</code>/<code>or</code> operators backwards, so when it calls <code>SetFileAttributes()</code> it ends up enabling <strong>all attributes other than <code>UNPINNED</code></strong>, which includes <code>SYSTEM</code> and <code>HIDDEN</code>. <code>UnpinFile()</code> is using the operators correctly.</p>
<p>Try this instead:</p>
<pre class="lang-pascal prettyprint-override"><code>const
  FILE_ATTRIBUTE_PINNED   = $00080000; // +P
  FILE_ATTRIBUTE_UNPINNED = $00100000; // +U

procedure PinFile(const FileName: string);
//PinFile('C:\Users\Allan\OneDrive\Test.docx');
var
  Attr: DWORD;
begin
  Attr := GetFileAttributes(PChar(FileName));
  if Attr = INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES then
    RaiseLastOSError;

  // -U  (remove unpinned) 
  Attr := Attr and not FILE_ATTRIBUTE_UNPINNED;

  // +P  (set pinned)
  Attr := Attr or FILE_ATTRIBUTE_PINNED;

  if not SetFileAttributes(PChar(FileName), Attr) then
    RaiseLastOSError;
end;

procedure UnpinFile(const FileName: string);
//UnpinFile('C:\Users\Allan\OneDrive\Test.docx');
var
  Attr: DWORD;
begin
  Attr := GetFileAttributes(PChar(FileName));
  if Attr = INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES then
    RaiseLastOSError;

  // -P  (remove pinned)
  Attr := Attr and not FILE_ATTRIBUTE_PINNED;

  // +U  (set unpinned)
  Attr := Attr or FILE_ATTRIBUTE_UNPINNED;

  if not SetFileAttributes(PChar(FileName), Attr) then
    RaiseLastOSError;
end;
</code></pre>
